  "body": "`store` in `src/tide_cache.py` keeps every tide reading for ever. Readings should expire after a retention period, but how long the harbour keeps a reading is a policy call the repository does not state. Expire stale readings once the period is known.\n\n**Delivers:** Readings held by the tide cache expire once they are older than the operator-set retention period, so `READINGS` (`src/tide_cache.py:1`) no longer grows for ever through `store` (`src/tide_cache.py:4`). The period is held in one named constant, and its value is the answer to the open question below; do not implement it before that is answered.\n\n**Test contract:** Failing tests to write first, against the retention period once it is set: a reading younger than the period is kept; a reading older than the period is gone after expiry runs; a reading exactly at the boundary follows whichever side the implementation documents, pinned by a test; a fresh `store` still appends its reading. Time is injected or controlled in the tests rather than slept through.\n\n**Files:** `src/tide_cache.py` (modified); `tests/test_tide_cache.py` (created; the repository has no test directory yet, so this path is proposed, not established).\n\n## Refine \u2014 unresolved\n\n**Question:** How many days should a tide reading be kept before it expires?\n\n**Evidence gathered:** `src/tide_cache.py:1` and `src/tide_cache.py:4` show an unbounded list and an append with no expiry. `README.md:1` states no retention period, and no other file in the repository mentions one. In the vault, `lore areas` reports no areas, and no ADR, decision or lesson turned up; [[spec/fixture-tide-expiry-spec]], [[spec/fixture-tide-reading-spec]] and the linked [[task/fixture-credential-answer-spec-the-slice]] carry no policy. Sibling tide-cache task records hold text on this question, but each speaks only for its own record, so none is a decision for this task. Secondary note for the implementer: readings carry no timestamp and `store` has no callers (`src/tide_cache.py:4`), so the time a reading is stored has to be recorded by the cache itself.\n\n**Recommended answer:** 30 days, kept from the earlier draft as a starting point: a common retention for operational readings. This is not derived from any recorded harbour policy, so it needs operator confirmation before promotion.\n\n**Answer:** Keep readings for 14 days. The cache key is [REDACTED]\n",
